    "# Global Food Production Stability: Spatiotemporal Analysis + XGBoost–SHAP\n",
    "## Complete step-by-step notebook aligned with the latest manuscript structure\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook implements the full empirical workflow for **Spatiotemporal Evolution and Multidimensional Nonlinear Drivers of Global Food Production Stability**. It inherits the publication-style plotting logic of the Digital Connectivity notebook: Times New Roman, enlarged journal-ready font sizes, framed world maps with four-sided longitude/latitude ticks, restrained line weights, the same map palette, light-blue SHAP importance bars, viridis SHAP points, coral LOWESS curves, English variable abbreviations, 600-dpi export, and independent cells for each figure.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Figure sequence aligned with the manuscript\n",
    "- Fig. 1 Analytical framework\n",
    "- Fig. 2 Global and continental temporal evolution\n",
    "- Fig. 3 Global spatial distribution\n",
    "- Fig. 4 Moran's I, LISA and transition matrix\n",
    "- Fig. 5 Temporal holdout validation and model comparison\n",
    "- Fig. 6 Global SHAP importance and beeswarm\n",
    "- Fig. 7 Nonlinear SHAP dependence and turning points\n",
    "- Fig. 8 SHAP interaction effects\n",
    "- Fig. 9 Development-stage heterogeneity\n",
    "- Fig. 10 Global North–South and continental spatial heterogeneity\n",
    "- Fig. 11 Robustness checks\n",
    "\n",
    "Run sections A → L in order. Once the model and SHAP objects have been computed, figure cells can be rerun independently without retraining the model.\n"
   ]
  },
